{"results":[{"index":0,"data":{"type":"issues","issues":[{"number":7490,"title":"Bug: Minimal reproduction for router.use() sub-app prototype corruption (#7427)","state":"closed","author":"garv-sanveria","labels":["bug","duplicate"],"createdAt":"2026-09-26T13:45:57Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T09:48:40Z","closedAt":"2026-09-27T02:54:32Z","body":"This is a minimal, runnable reproduction for issue #7427. \n\nWhen an `express()` sub-app is mounted via `router.use()` instead of `app.use()`, the `req` and `res` prototypes are swapped by `app.handle` but never restored when the sub-app calls `next()`. \n\nAs a result, any middleware that runs *after* the sub-app finishes will silently inherit the sub-app's configuration (like `trust proxy`) instead of the parent app's configuration.\n\n### Expected Behavior\nAfter a sub-app mounted on a router calls `next()`, the `req` prototype should be restored so subsequent middleware uses the parent app's settings.\n\n### Reproduction Script\n```js\nconst express = require('express');\n\nconst app = express();\nconst router = express.Router();\nconst subApp = express();\n\n// Parent app does NOT trust proxy\napp.set('trust proxy', false);\n\n// Sub app DOES trust proxy\nsubApp.set('trust proxy', true);\nsubApp.use((req, res, next) => {\n  // Do nothing, just pass back to the parent router\n  next(); \n});\n\n// BUG TRIGGER: Mounting subApp via router instead of app.use\nrouter.use('/test', subApp);\napp.use(router);\n\napp.use('/test', (req, res) => {\n  // Expected: false (Parent app setting)\n  // Actual: true (Leaked sub-app setting!)\n  res.json({ \n    isProxyTrusted: req.app.get('trust proxy') \n  });\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () => {\n  console.log('Listening on 3000. Run: curl http://localhost:3000/test');\n});\n\n\n\nSystem Info\nExpress version: 4.21.2\nNode.js version: 20.x\nOS: MacOS","comments":[{"id":"5851925106","bodyPagination":{"charOffset":0,"charLength":389,"totalChars":389,"hasMore":false},"body":"Hi! I'd like to work on this issue. I understand the bug: when a sub-app is mounted via router.use() instead of app.use(), the req and res prototypes are swapped by app.handle but never restored when the sub-app calls next(), causing the parent's settings (like trust proxy) to leak.\n\nI'll investigate app.handle and add a test to verify the fix. Could I be assigned to this issue? Thanks!","createdAt":"2026-09-27T02:20:45Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T02:20:45Z","commentType":"discussion","user":"dimitrimbesseu-arch"},{"id":"5852108128","bodyPagination":{"charOffset":0,"charLength":1031,"totalChars":1031,"hasMore":false},"body":"Thanks for the reproducer @garv-sanveria. Usually when you have something to add that is related to an existing issue (such as a minimised reproducer) this should be done in that issue to make it easier to find. There is (at least) one reproducer that is not public (it was reported in a rejected security advisory), but this may be useful to others<!-- no, it won't, because 7427 will probably be closed as won't fix -->.\n\nI'll close this as a duplicate, but feel free to add a comment with your reproducer to #7427. That being said, my personal opinion is that #7427 is **not a bug**, because such configuration is simply not supported.\n\n@dimitrimbesseu-arch in general, we don't assign people to issues. If you see an issue that you can solve, please check if there are no related PRs and then open yours (if solving such issue requires code changes). In this case there already is one (and another that was closed as a duplicate) and the issue may not be something that we consider an issue (this is still open for discussion).","createdAt":"2026-09-27T02:54:32Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T02:54:32Z","commentType":"discussion","user":"krzysdz"}],"contentPagination":{"comments":{"currentPage":1,"itemsPerPage":30,"totalComments":2,"returnedComments":2,"hasMore":false}}}]}}]}
